--- a/tests/host/kernel-performance/README.md
+++ b/tests/host/kernel-performance/README.md
@@ -68,3 +68,18 @@ addresses, incomplete blocks and whole-arena comparisons. A host-only counter
 limits `DesBit` calls to the initial/final permutations: 128 per DES pass,
 versus 1,408 before combining S-box substitution with the P permutation.
 The work bound is deterministic; it does not claim native throughput.
+
+Modular exponentiation padding regression:
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/host/kernel-performance/modexp.py SOURCE_ROOT OUTPUT --optimized --sanitized
+```
+
+The actual production arithmetic is compared to Python `pow` for zero, small,
+full-width and high-word exponent cases. Whole and shifted Result aliases of
+every operand, complete output canaries, untouched other operands, rejection
+and forced allocation failure are checked. The padding budget keeps products,
+bit reduction steps and scratch bytes bounded by the one-word numerical inputs,
+independent of their caller word count. `--sanitized` additionally compiles the
+364-check public vector fixture with 32-bit ASan/UBSan. Native public guest
+qualification remains required; host counters are not throughput measurements.
